<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Altech H1 headline earnings drop.</title>
<headline>Altech H1 headline earnings drop.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1996-10-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Half year ended August 31</p>
<p>			(million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>Headline shr, attrib (cts)  313.3 vs 388.6</p>
<p>    Shr, attrib (cts)     373.5	 vs 12.1 loss</p>
<p>    Div (cts)		 nil	   vs same</p>
<p>    Attrib income	   38.04	 vs 1.22 loss</p>
<p>    Exceptional item	5.42	  vs 54.06 loss</p>
<p>    Income before exceps, tax 73.35   vs 69.51</p>
<p>    Pre-tax		   78.35	 vs 15.45</p>
<p>    Tax			 25.59	 vs 20.53</p>
<p>Outside shareholders interest 15.13 vs 3.54 gain</p>
<p>    Turnover		  963.29	vs 714.86</p>
<p>Full name: Allied Technologies Ltd</p>
<p>NOTE - South African electronics group Altech said that the group was turning around and this process is expected to continue in the second half, despite an increase in competition.</p>
<p>&quot;Market indications are that the economic climate will deteriorate during the enxt six month period, but the directors are confident of real growth for Altech,&quot; the firm said in a statement.</p>
<p>The exceptional loss last time was due to a write-off of industrialisation expenditure, while the gain in 1996 was due to a surplus on disposal of investments.</p>
<p>The group declares a single dividend at year-end only.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
